types.description:
One row of a connector's entities namespace: an entity the connector imported from its source system, staged until a merge writes it to the graph.

`context` is free-form JSON. It holds the connector's own read-only source data, plus, on `previewConnectorEntities` responses only, a reserved `__preview` bucket the server computes for each row:

```json
{
  "area": 42.5,
  "number": "B1-204",
  "__preview": {
    "tags": ["selected", "updated", "firstSeen"],
    "fields": {
      "name":  { "display": "DEFAULT", "diverged": true },
      "floor": { "display": "RULE", "graphCheck": "UNRESOLVED" }
    },
    "selection": { "display": "SETTLED" },
    "selectable": true,
    "missingRequired": [],
    "duplicateUnique": [],
    "removedFields": ["legacyCode"],
    "contextChanged": true,
    "baseTypeChanged": true,
    "rulesError": { "scope": "entity", "message": "Cannot read properties of undefined", "line": 3, "column": 12 }
  }
}
```

`tags` values: `selected`, `added`, `updated`, `deleted`, `missing`, `unresolved`, `firstSeen`. `display` values, in precedence order: `CONFLICT`, `RULE`, `UNSAVED`, `DEFAULT`, `SETTLED`. `diverged`, `removedFields`, `contextChanged` and `baseTypeChanged` appear only when true or non-empty, and say why an `updated` row changed. `rulesError` appears only when the merge rule failed for the row: `scope` is `entity` for this row only, or `rule` for the whole rule, on every row. Keys starting with `__` are reserved for the platform.
